er  nineteen-year-old julius jones was  arrested his family says eyewitness  descriptions did not match julius who at  the time had a shaved head they also say  he was home at the time of the murder  [Music]  wednesday his mother surrounded by  supporters pleaded for his release the  truth will set you free we talk about  justice justice for whom  justice for all of us  earlier this month oklahoma's pardon and  parole board recommended his sentence be  commuted asking the governor to change  it to life in prison with the  possibility of parole the board chairman  said i believe in death penalty cases  there should be no doubt and put simply  i have doubts in this case i am not the  person responsible for taking mr house  life but paul howell's family says  that's not true we spoke to howell's  daughter rachel before the board made  their clemency recommendation i want to  be a voice for my dad because  he was an innocent man  taking his kids to get ice cream with my  aunt and he was murdered  in front of me and my sister and my aunt  all for a car  and he never got a say in this there's  overwhelming amount of evidence of his  guilt julius jones fate is now in the  hands of oklahoma's republican governor  kevin stitt who so far has only met with  the howell family this is the first  death row clemency case he's faced  antoinette says she'll be at the prison  later today will you go inside  i have to i have to be there for my  brother  i would want him to be there for me  you're taking a lot on yourself  why  because he's worth it his life is worth  it his life has always been worth the  fight  police have set up barricades at the  governor's mansion just in case there's  any unrest we've seen a number of extra  troopers brought here to the state  capitol there are expected rallies at  the prison as well as here at in  oklahoma city if the governor does  nothing right now the execution will go  as planned it's set for 4 p.m  central time gail  maria this is a heartbreaking story on  so many levels thank you so much listen  we're all very sorry that paul howe lost  his life  that's the main thing but number two  there still seem to be so many questions  you have the parole board chairman  saying that he has doubts in the case  i don't understand why the governor said  he'll meet with the why he will not meet  with the jones family when he's met with  the howell family yeah it's a lot to  process the expert's sitting here but  the people who've looked at the case  closely seem to have doubts and that  should go a long way but but you're  right i mean it's heinous the crime but  yeah also heinous to put to death a  person who may not have done it yeah and  not to be dismissive to the victim's  family like you're saying we understand  that but when the parole bird parole  board is speaking out it's almost like  when do you decide not to listen to them  yeah because in other instances you  listen to every word that they have to  say about cases you know my first  thought was for the victims and the  victim's family questions looking at  julius jones and there's too many  questions here there's doubt

